From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:26:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Adjust upstream XSAs to the LCM code

The commit that changed the parameter
from Unix.file_descr to Unix.file_descr option is not present in 8.3

(https://github.com/xapi-project/xen-api/commit/ac4ff6d3781d0bb20102355b789ad7fd7b02f5a4)

Adjust the XSA unit test patch - use an arbitrary fd instead of None. This is
safe since no forwarding takes place in the unit tests anyway.

Signed-off-by: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
---
 ocaml/tests/test_task_ownership.ml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ocaml/tests/test_task_ownership.ml b/ocaml/tests/test_task_ownership.ml
index c81be0b50..f73021ecb 100644
--- a/ocaml/tests/test_task_ownership.ml
+++ b/ocaml/tests/test_task_ownership.ml
@@ -311,7 +311,7 @@ let dispatch ?task ?(supports_async = true) ~session_id () =
     Server_helpers.do_dispatch ~session_id supports_async "Test.call"
       (fun ~__context:_ -> ran := true)
       (fun () -> Rpc.Null)
-      None
+      Unix.stdout
       (request_with_task_header ?task ~session_id ())
       "test_do_dispatch" `Sync true
   in
